  <h2 id="s-1">How to report a lost item</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Click <strong>Report an item</strong> in the top-right of any page.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>I lost something</strong>.</li>
    <li>Give the item a short title — for example "Black leather wallet".</li>
    <li>Pick a category and the location where you last had it.</li>
    <li>Enter the date you lost it. It cannot be in the future.</li>
    <li>Describe it in at least 20 characters. Mention colour, brand, marks.</li>
    <li>Submit. You will get a reference number like <code>LF-2026-0007</code>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Expected result:</strong> your report is public and other users can match it
  against found items.</p>

  <h2 id="s-2">How to report a found item</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Click <strong>Report an item</strong> and choose <strong>I found
    something</strong>.</li>
    <li>Fill in the same fields as above.</li>
    <li>In the <strong>Holding location</strong> box, say where the item is being
    kept. Example: "CCS Dean's office, 2nd floor."</li>
    <li>Submit. Note down the reference number.</li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Expected result:</strong> the item appears under Found reports, and
  its owner can file a claim.</p>

  <h2 id="s-3">How to search for an item</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Use the search box on the home page or click <strong>Reports</strong> in
    the nav.</li>
    <li>Type a keyword — part of a name, brand, or colour works.</li>
    <li>Optional: narrow by kind (lost / found), category, location, status, or
    date range.</li>
    <li>Press Enter or click <strong>Apply filters</strong>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="s-4">How to file a claim</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the found report you believe is yours.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>This is mine — file a claim</strong>.</li>
    <li>Sign in with your student number and 4-digit PIN if you have not yet.</li>
    <li>Write at least 30 characters of proof — where and when you lost it, and
    how you would recognise it.</li>
    <li>List at least 30 characters of distinguishing features.</li>
    <li>Submit. You will see a claim confirmation page.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="s-5">How to check the status of your reports</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Click <strong>My Reports</strong> in the nav.</li>
    <li>Sign in with your student number and PIN.</li>
    <li>You will see your reports and your claims.</li>
    <li>Each row shows the current status — open, matched, claimed, returned, or
    archived.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="s-6">What happens after a claim is approved</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>The person who posted the report approves your claim. Every other pending claim on the same report is
    automatically rejected.</li>
    <li>The report status changes to <strong>claimed</strong>.</li>
    <li>They contact you to arrange the handover.</li>
    <li>Bring your student ID when you collect. The person handing it over records who
    received it and when.</li>
    <li>The report status changes to <strong>returned</strong>.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="s-7">What to do when something goes wrong</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>I forgot my PIN.</strong> Contact the IT office in person with
    your student ID. This is a demo constraint; Week 11 replaces PINs with real
    passwords.</li>
    <li><strong>I filed a report by mistake.</strong> Open it and click Withdraw
    while its status is still <em>open</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>The system shows an error page.</strong> Note the reference ID on
    the page and email it to the IT office. Do not screenshot; the ID is enough.</li>
    <li><strong>My claim was rejected but I think it is really mine.</strong>
    Contact Student Affairs. Bring whatever evidence you have.</li>
  </ul>

